      "score": 39,
      "reasoning": "This is Mode A: the report provides quantitative estimates for cumulative loss, early/late rates, acceleration, and 2023 loss. Its cumulative and period-average estimates are fairly close to the published values, but uncertainty treatment is acknowledged as underestimated, the 2023 maximum is substantially weaker (−460 ± 71 versus −548 ± 120 Gt), and it omits the required quantitative comparison showing glaciers exceed Greenland and Antarctic ice-sheet contributions."
     },
     {
      "index": 1,
      "type": "image",
      "weight": 0.1,
      "score": 28,
      "reasoning": "This is Mode A because the criterion specifies quantitative regional contribution and relative-loss percentages. The report approximately identifies the dominant absolute contributors, though Alaska, Greenland, and Southern Andes shares differ from the reference and the Canadian Arctic is split; critically, it never computes or visualizes loss relative to 2000 ice volume, substituting specific mass-change rates, which are not equivalent."
     },
     {
      "index": 2,
      "type": "image",
      "weight": 0.2,
      "score": 22,
      "reasoning": "This is Mode A because the criterion specifies quantitative method-to-method biases and uncertainties. The report provides partial comparisons, but its altimetry (+0.04) and gravimetry (−0.03) differences do not reproduce the target values, omits uncertainty estimates and the glaciological bias/range, and improperly combines DEM and glaciological observations; the visual also lacks the target’s full regional uncertainty comparison."
     },
     {
      "index": 3,
      "type": "image",
      "weight": 0.3,
      "score": 0,
      "reasoning": "Mode A. None of the AI-generated figures compare observations with GlacierMIP2/CMIP6 projections or show low/high-emission pathways through 2040–2100; the required 2040 exceedance, 2100 loss ranges, and AR5/SROCC/AR6 percentage comparisons are absent. The cumulative observational plot ends in 2023 and therefore does not reproduce the target figure or criterion."
     }
